# Nour configuration
#
# Nour is offline-first and has no backend: prayer times, Qibla and the Quran
# Mushaf are all computed on-device, and the app declares no INTERNET
# permission. There are no API keys, no server endpoints and no accounts.
#
# Release signing is the only thing that needs credentials, and those are read
# from the environment (never from a file in the repo):
#   KEYSTORE_PATH   path to the upload keystore (.jks)
#   STORE_PASSWORD  keystore password
#   KEY_ALIAS       key alias (default: upload)
#   KEY_PASSWORD    key password
#
# Without those variables, release builds fall back to the debug keystore so
# `assembleRelease` still works for local verification. That fallback must
# never be used for a published build.
